course: dictionary
lesson: 11844
title: The bloodstream
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The bloodstream is the blood that flows round and round your body. It travels through tubes called blood vessels: arteries, veins and capillaries.
explain: Read the words around it. «The heart pumps blood into the bloodstream.» The heart pumps, and blood is moving, so the bloodstream must be the moving blood. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "The heart pumps blood into the moving blood" still makes sense.
explain: «The bloodstream carries oxygen and food to every part of the body.» Carries tells you the bloodstream moves things around. It also takes waste away, so it works in both directions.
fact: The bloodstream is the blood moving round the body through the blood vessels.
fact: Blood vessels are arteries, veins and capillaries.
fact: The heart pumps blood into the bloodstream.
fact: The bloodstream carries oxygen and food to every part of the body, and takes waste away.
fact: Medicines, alcohol and drugs can get into the bloodstream, which is why health lessons talk about them.
exercise: «The heart pumps blood into the bloodstream.» What is the bloodstream? | The tube that carries air into the lungs | The skin that covers the body | The bones that hold up the body | *The blood that flows round the body through the blood vessels
exercise: «The bloodstream carries oxygen and food to every part of the body.» What does the bloodstream carry? | Letters and parcels | Sounds and songs | *Oxygen and food | Sand and stones
exercise: What does the bloodstream take away from the body? | Food | Heat | Oxygen | *Waste
test: «Harmful drugs can get into the bloodstream.» Where can harmful drugs get to? | Only the skin | Out of the mouth | *Into the blood moving round the body | Into the hair
test: Which phrase means the blood moving through your body? | The skeleton | The lungs | *The bloodstream | The stomach
exam: A doctor says, «The medicine is in the bloodstream.» What does this mean? | *The medicine is in the blood moving round the body | The medicine is outside the skin | The medicine is in the bones | The medicine is in the stomach only
